        "argument_status": "invalid",
        "statement_status": "refuted",
        "decisive_reason": "The proposed obligation preserves the source distinction between each fixed $j$ and the growing maximum. On a one-point probability space, take $m_n=n$ and $X_{n,j}=\\mathbf{1}_{\\{j=n\\}}$ for $1\\le j\\le n$. For every fixed $j$, $X_{n,j}=0$ for every $n>j$, so the hypotheses hold. Yet $\\max_{1\\le j\\le n}|X_{n,j}|=1$ for every $n$, giving $P(\\max_{1\\le j\\le n}|X_{n,j}|>1/2)=1$. Thus line 16 does not follow from line 15, and the counterexample refutes C001 itself.",
